  "question": {
    "text": "Magnetic field in a plane electromagnetic wave is given by,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. Expression for corresponding electric field will be:<br /><br />(Where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> is speed of light)",
